       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1,600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily dose of ibuprofen. A single 1,600 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n\n- **Usual maximum:** The maximum is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use in adults, given as 400\u2013800 mg per dose. Doses above that add no analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit. They do raise the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, cardiovascular events, and fluid retention or hypertension.\n- **Possible typo:** The intended dose may have been 400 mg or 800 mg, or the total may have been meant as 1,600 mg/day.\n\nHere are some typical regimens for a 70 kg adult with normal renal and hepatic function. Use the one that fits the indication.\n- **Mild to moderate pain:** 400 mg PO every 4\u20136 hours as needed.\n- **Inflammatory or musculoskeletal conditions:** 600\u2013800 mg PO three times daily (max 3,200 mg/day).\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you intended, ideally with your supervising resident or attending. Once you do, I'll enter the order."
